[00:02.300]Lesson 121 | 第121课
[00:05.700]I bought two expensive dictionaries here half an hour ago, but I forgot /fəˈɡɒt/ to take them with me. | 半小时前我在这里买了两本昂贵的词典，但我忘了带走它们。
[00:14.300]Who served /sɜːvd/ you, sir? | 先生，是谁为您服务的？
[00:17.000]The lady who is standing behind the counter /ˈkaʊntə/. | 站在柜台后面的那位女士。
[00:20.700]Which books did you buy? | 您买了哪些书？
[00:23.000]The books which are on the counter /ˈkaʊntə/. | 柜台上的那些书。
[00:26.700]Did you serve /sɜːv/ this gentleman /ˈdʒentlmən/ half an hour ago, Miss Roberts? | 罗伯茨小姐，半小时前您为这位先生服务过吗？
[00:31.300]He says he's the man who bought these books. | 他说他就是买这些书的人。
[00:34.700]I can't remember, sir. | 先生，我不记得了。
[00:37.300]The man whom I served /sɜːvd/ was wearing a hat. | 我服务的那个人戴着帽子。
[00:41.600]Have you got a hat, sir? | 先生，您有帽子吗？
[00:43.700]Yes, I have. | 是的，我有。
[00:45.600]Would you put it on, please? | 请您戴上好吗？
[00:48.000]All right. | 好的。
[00:50.400]Is this the man that you served /sɜːvd/, Miss Roberts? | 罗伯茨小姐，这就是您服务过的那个人吗？
[00:54.000]Yes, sir. I recognize /ˈrekəɡnaɪz/ him now. | 是的，先生。我现在认出他了。
